<title>USA: HP sees &quot;extremely challenging&quot; market.</title>
<headline>HP sees &quot;extremely challenging&quot; market.</headline>
<dateline>PALO ALTO, Calif. 1997-02-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hewlett-Packard Co (HP) will manage its expenses and assets carefully in the coming months in expectation of an &quot;extremely challenging&quot; competitive market, Lewis Platt, the company's chairman, president and chief executive, said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>HP said its orders for its first fiscal quarter ended January 31 rose by nine percent to $11.0 billion. It said the rise would have been about two percentage points higher without the effects of currency exchange rates.  </p>
<p>Some analysts had expected slightly better growth in orders.</p>
<p>Platt said growth was &quot;a bit slower than we would have liked&quot; despite a difficult comparison with the year-ago period.</p>
</text>
